  "title": "Lauren NDE 6774",
  "date": "6/24/06",
  "content": "I remember being taken into the operating room for a cesarean section but remember nothing after being given medication. My epidural was not working at the level needed for surgery and so I was given general anesthesia. I remember nothing other than flying out of body through the top of my head. I floated around for a bit, everything was blue and was I unsure where I was. I looked down at my son in his incubator and remember thinking 'Am I dead? If I am dead, it's okay because the baby is alright.' (I later saw my son's picture from the same point in time it matched exactly what I saw, even though the incubator was on the other side of the curtain.) I floated out of the hospital and remember looking at the yellow bricks outside. I was flying around and I started looking for my great-grandmother, who was terminally ill at the time, to see if she had 'arrived yet'. I just felt free and peaceful, until sometime later (not sure how long in actual minutes, just 'a while'). I floated back down and then I don't remember anything else until I woke up.",
